CREATED:20260921T135439Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T135904Z
UID:10004477-1795006800-1795010400@events.ackland.org
SUMMARY:Tour: A Closer Look at Ackland Upstairs
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an hour-long conversation about the connections between Asian art at the Ackland and scholarly research in Asian and Middle Eastern History\, featuring Dr. Morgan Pitelka (Asian Studies and History)\, and Dr. Elizabeth Manekin\, head of university programs and academic projects at the Ackland. \nFree\, but space is limited; registration required below. \nThis event is part of UNC–Chapel Hill’s Campus Life Experience (CLE) program. Students who attend can scan the QR code provided at the event to receive CLE credit.
URL:https://events.ackland.org/event/nov2026-tour-a-closer-look-at-ackland-upstairs/
LOCATION:Ackland Art Museum\, 101 S. Columbia Street\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:Tours
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.ackland.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/i-q6DxKKS-X3.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Ackland Art Museum
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261119T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261119T160000
DTSTAMP:20261113T151442Z
CREATED:20261014T165219Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261113T151442Z
UID:10004852-1795100400-1795104000@events.ackland.org
SUMMARY:An Ackland Odyssey
DESCRIPTION:This program is now FULL. To be added to our WAITLIST\, please email acklandRSVP@unc.edu. \n  \nHow have artists represented the characters from Homer’s Odyssey through the centuries? How do images translate and adapt the words from this epic poem for new\, diverse audiences? \nProfessors Timothy Shea and Hérica Valladares\, both from UNC-Chapel Hill’s Department of Classics with adjunct appointments in the Department of Art and Art History\, will lead a seminar-style discussion focusing on works from the museum’s collection\, ranging from an ancient Greek vase fragment to a twentieth-century lithograph by American artist Benton Spruance. \nFree\, registration required below. \n  \nThis event is part of UNC–Chapel Hill’s Campus Life Experience (CLE) program. Students who attend can scan the QR code provided at the event to receive CLE credit.
URL:https://events.ackland.org/event/an-ackland-odyssey/
LOCATION:Ackland Art Museum\, 101 S. Columbia Street\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.ackland.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/77.6.10.jpg
END:VEVENT
