SUMMARY:Semester Revue: Student Research and Responses to the Collection
DESCRIPTION:Each semester\, the Ackland Art Museum works with thousands of UNC-Chapel Hill students through courses and internships. The Semester Revue offers a glimpse into the quality and variety of the students’ research\, projects\, and performances. Come learn about the collection and see it anew through their short\, dynamic presentations. \nFree public program; no registration required. \n  \nThe Ackland Semester Revue is part of UNC-Chapel Hill’s Campus Life Experience program. Scan the QR code at the event for CLE credit.
URL:https://events.ackland.org/event/semester-revue-student-research-and-responses-to-the-collection/
LOCATION:Ackland Art Museum\, 101 S. Columbia Street\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
CATEGORIES:Special Programs,Talks
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.ackland.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/GetImage2-scaled.jpeg
END:VEVENT
